NAME
    rm - remove files and directories (currently suspended)

SYNOPSIS
    rm [-r] <path>

SUSPENDED
    rm currently refuses all invocations and exits with status 1. It was
    parked when the shell sandbox still encompassed install binaries;
    although '/' is now rooted at EmuSen's home directory (see hier(7)),
    the safeguard remains in place. The section below describes the
    command's intended interface.

DESCRIPTION
    Removes a file or, with -r, a directory and its contents inside the
    shell sandbox without prompting. Removing the sandbox root itself is
    refused.

OPTIONS
    -r  Remove directories and their contents recursively.

EXAMPLES
    rm /Logs/scratch.txt
    rm -r /Logs/OldRun

EXIT STATUS
    1   Always fails while suspended.

SEE ALSO
    mv(1), cp(1), hier(7)
